foreign  welcome back to Harry Potter Theory who  was more powerful Sirius Black or  Dolores Umbridge for those of us who  think this question has an obvious  answer we might blindly claim Sirius as  the mightier wizard but others who  consider this question carefully know  that it's not as simple as black and  white Sirius Black was one of the  greatest Duelists in the entire Order of  the Phoenix but Dolores Umbridge was a  cunning strategist and in her own way  was able to defeat even Albus Dumbledore  So today we're going to take a look at  these two prominent members of The  Wizarding World and figure out who was  more powerful how we'll do it now  whenever you compare Wizards and witches  to see who is more powerful there are a  few different ways to go about it we can  just stack up their list of dueling  opponents and see which one is defeated  the most powerful wizard or witch but  that doesn't quite capture a full  picture on the other side of the debate  we could just rifle through Cirrus  blacks and Dolores umbridge's  proficiency with spells and potions but  that too doesn't quite seem like enough  either to really get to the answer we're  going to take a holistic approach we'll  break down these two opponents in three  different categories one magical Feats  two dueling and three intangibles after  taking a look at each of these we should  be able to get to the bottom of this  matter and figure out who really was the  more powerful magic user between them  magical Feats when we look at Sirius  Black's magical feeds there's simply no  shortage of achievements to Marvel ants  ziris hails from one of the oldest pure  blood families in Britain and even  though Wizard's pureblood Heritage  didn't necessarily have any great  bearing on their magical abilities  Sirius was certainly steeped in magical  lore from an early age perhaps that's  what made him such a great member of the  Marauders a group of four young Hogwarts  friends who were all equally obsessed  with perfecting spells and disrupting  classes Sirius became an accomplished  transfigurationist when he was just a  teenager a skilled potioneer by just his  fifth year in Hogwarts and even helped  to construct the Marauders map which had  become the basis for many of Harry  Potter's adventures in the decades that  followed but sirius's greatest magical  feat was certainly his escape from  Azkaban that horrid prison inhabited by  the soul-leating Dementors had never  lost an inmate in a breakout and until  bharti Crouch Jr was revealed to be  alive and well Sirius Black was the very  first one in all of recorded history but  the simple fact that he escaped Azkaban  is somehow the least interesting part of  it because he did so with relative ease  even though he had been prison for over  a decade and had ample time to  transfigure into his animagus form black  had never tried to use it to escape with  only a thought black was able to  transform into a black dog and since he  never registered that skill with the  ministry of magic none of the Dementors  or other Ministry officers would have  known the menji mat was actually Sirius  Black so using his skills in  Transfiguration black simply changed  into his animagus and walked out of  Azkaban and swam across the sea to the  mainland and when we turn our attention  to Dolores umbridge's magical feeds  we'll find an equally impressive  although less bombastic list of  achievements in hindsight after Umbridge  was locked away for good many of the  Wizards and witches of Harry Potter's  generation looked back on umbrage with  disdain and for good reason she was an  absolute Tyrant during her time at  Hogwarts and tortured the students at  every child she had but Harry and his  peers dislike from bridge has led to the  rise of a rumor that she wasn't a very  great witch which isn't entirely Fair  she was one of the highest ranking  members of the ministry of magic and in  time the headmistress of Hogwarts I'm  sure when compared to other professors  at the school like Minerva McGonagall or  Severus Snape  Umbridge wasn't up to snuff but Snape  and McGonagall were among the greatest  Wizards and witches of the entire  Century so holding umbrage next to them  isn't giving her a fair Shake if we set  our sights a little bit lower and  measure Umbridge fairly we'll find that  she was a decent witch in her own right  she created the black quill which was  able to painfully carve words into the  tomb of students hands and her use of  the fire making spell and shield spell  certainly didn't make her look like a  subpar wedge as she used them in combat  and classroom management but her  greatest feat was her ability to  weaponize Dementors she set them loose  on Harry and dursley which put Hogwarts  on a course for the eventual dismissal  of Albus Dumbledore even though the  ministry of magic had a system for  controlling Dementors one that remains a  mystery until this day it was rare for  an individual to utilize Dementors on  their own and not only did Dolores  Umbridge do that but she managed to  weaponize the Dementors without letting  too many other members of the ministry  in on her plan dueling but let's take a  step away from their magical Feats and  look at their dueling skills we'll start  with Sirius Black again because he is  the longest and perhaps most impressive  record when it comes to Dueling this era  the greatest combatants were either  members of the Order of the Phoenix or  members of the Death Eaters  sure there were professional Duelists  all around the globe but their Jewels  had rules judges and a strict system  when the Order of the Phoenix went to  war against Voldemort both sides knew  the death was a certain possibility  and even after being imprisoned for over  a decade the experience from his time in  the Order of the Phoenix served Sirius  Black yet again the battle of the  Department of Mysteries black easily  defeated Antonin dolahov in their fight  and immediately after pushed Bellatrix  Lestrange to the absolute Brink  during that final fight when Sirius  Black fought his cousin one-on-one black  couldn't help but gloat at his obvious  superiority in dueling but that brief  moment of arrogance would cost him his  life as a spell from bellatrix's wand  caught black Square in his chest and  pushed him through the Gateway of death  again after taking a look at Sirius  Black's accomplishments and his failed  it's hard to look at Dolores umbridge's  without seeing an obvious Gap unlike  Sirius Black Umbridge never spent her  childhood getting into fights with her  fellow witches and wizards as a member  of the Marauders black would regularly  stomp around the grounds of Hogwarts and  stir up travel with other children like  an unwitting Severus Snape although  those years in school might have seemed  like misguided youth or Worse bullying  Sirius Black certainly earned enough  experience to make him a decent duelist  by his seventh year and once he joined  to the Order of the Phoenix his  abilities only improved but Umbridge as  we've already stated didn't have the  same upbringing and she simply doesn't  have the same level of dueling opponents  in her past besides her one attempt to  defeat Albus Dumbledore in a duel there  actually isn't much that we can go by  she was obviously quite skilled with  Transfiguration unlike Sirius Black who  used that craft to conjure an animagus  unbridged used Transfiguration for her  typical darker form of magic she could  use her expertise to cast the  incarcerous spell which she used to  nearly murder a centaur in the Forbidden  Forest conjuration is a skill reserved  for the most talented witches and  wizards if she used similarly Sinister  magic during a jewel against Sirius  blank or another witch or wizard then  she could very well surprise them and  capture a victory  intangibles when we look at Sirius Black  and Dolores Umbridge it's not as simple  as their spell work or their dueling  skills there's a greater element of  intangibles the things that simply  weighed or measured and that's where  Dolores Umbridge seems to excel because  for Sirius Black his magical abilities  are all pretty straightforward he uses  them directly in combat against the dark  Wizards serving the Lord Voldemort  Dolores Umbridge is rarely that direct  she uses her magic to serve a simple end  her own rise through the politics of The  Wizarding World and in that Pursuit she  rarely seemed to abuse her magical  powers when she wanted to impose her  will on other teachers at Hogwarts she  didn't use her wand to do so she  artfully maneuvered the ministry of  magic to defeat faculty members on her  behalf and when she wanted to Target  troubled students she didn't suddenly  round them up with a great show of  forceful magic like a proper dark wizard  would instead Like a Surgeon she used  her own dark Creations like the black  quill or the occasional use of the  cruciatus curse to impose her will and  while Dolores Umbridge might not have  wowed anyone with her use of magic she  certainly got what she wanted she Rose  through the ranks of the ministry all  the way to the very top by Voldemort's  time all of that despite the fact that  her father was a humble janitor at the  ministry a fact that would have made any  other ambitious Ministry worker the  subject of non-stop ridicule but  Umbridge never allowed it and in all  likelihood disposed of those who even  attempted to make fun of her Heritage  Umbridge also had the rarest theme of  being a witch who defeated Dumbledore  again not through the ways you might  have expected but that doesn't really  matter in the end Umbridge found a way  de deliberately or through luck to  unseat Alba's Dumbledore as Headmaster  something that Voldemort couldn't even  do and to be completely honest something  at Voldemort didn't have the patience to  figure out conclusion so when we finally  try to answer this question who was more  powerful Sirius Black or Dolores  Umbridge I think the answer lies with  you what do you value more in your  wizard if you prefer a duelist who could  take on almost anyone in a fair fight  and come out the Victor then you'd  probably think Sirius Black was the more  powerful wizard but if you're a bit more  holistic and think about what either one  was able to achieve you might be  surprised by the fact that Umbridge did  so much I know I was personally I'm  giving it to Umbridge and that's it for  this video if you enjoy the content  please like the video and subscribe to  the channel until next time remember if  you want to know what a man's like take  a good look at how he treats his  inferiors not his equals  [Music]  thank you

